# conn scope 100 — take the WebSocket connection on /connect.
#
# Everything past this point is trusted for the life of the session: the
# stack decided, once, that this connection may bind a service inside its
# workspace. That is the model — a binding is a capability the stack grants
# here, not a bypass, and the chassis carries the bytes afterward without
# running the stack per frame.
#
# A real deployment gates this the way any upgrade is gated (a session
# cookie, an Origin allowlist, `state.user`); this example keeps it open so
# it runs with nothing configured. The subsequent messages run at
# conn/_websocket/0.
WHEN @websocket.upgrade == true && @web.req.url.path == "/connect"
  EXEC "txco://websocket/accept"
